  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Doing something for someone else",
     "texto": [
      "**て + あげます**: you do something for someone: **にほんご を おしえて あげました** (I taught him/her Japanese). If someone else does it for you, **て + くれます**: **ちず を かいて くれました** (they drew me a map).",
      "**あげる** can sound presumptuous if used with someone of higher status; in that case it is usually better to describe the action without this verb."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Receiving a favour",
     "texto": [
      "**て + もらいます** = I receive a favour from someone: **てつだって もらいました** (I was helped).",
      "To thank someone for a favour, say **〜て くれて ありがとう** (thanks for doing it)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
